{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"touch-and-force","name":"Touch, force and weight","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"Parts that feel what presses on them, from the real physics: a touch pad (TTP223), a force pad (FSR), a limit switch and a robot bumper, a slide potentiometer you push with the ball or drag, and a kitchen scale (load cell + HX711) that weighs what you put on it. Includes HX711.h.","category":"Sensors","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// Touch, force and weight: each reads part.touch(id), what the physics says presses on a solid piece\r\n// of its shape (force in newtons, and whether the pushing ball touches it).\r\n\r\n// TTP223: a capacitive pad. A finger (the ball) or anything resting on it counts as a touch.\r\nbench.device('ttp223', (part) => {\r\n  const pad = part.touch('pad');\r\n  const btn = part.control('touch');\r\n  const toggle = part.params.mode === 'toggle';\r\n  let powered = false, touched = false, out = false, count = 0;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      powered = v >= 2;\r\n      const now = pad.hand || pad.touching || btn.down;\r\n      if (now && !touched) { count++; if (toggle) out = !out; }\r\n      touched = now;\r\n      if (!toggle) out = touched;\r\n      if (!powered) { io.release('SIG'); io.draw(0); return; }\r\n      io.drive('SIG', out ? v : 0, 1);\r\n      io.draw(out ? 0.002 : 0.0015);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\r\n      return [`${touched ? 'touched' : 'not touched'}: SIG ${out ? 'HIGH' : 'LOW'}`, `${count} touches`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// FSR 402 with a 10k resistor to GND: AO = VCC * 10k / (10k + R), R falls as the force grows\r\n// (about 30k at 1 N, 3k at 10 N; open circuit when nothing presses).\r\nbench.device('fsr', (part) => {\r\n  const pad = part.touch('pad');\r\n  const hand = part.control('press');\r\n  let powered = false, force = 0, ao = 0;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      powered = v >= 2;\r\n      // (the ball touching it presses with about 2 N: it's a fingertip)\r\n      force = Math.max(pad.force, pad.hand ? 2 : 0, hand.value);\r\n      const r = force > 0.02 ? 30000 / Math.pow(force, 0.95) : 1e7;\r\n      ao = powered ? (v * 10000) / (10000 + r) : 0;\r\n      if (!powered) { io.release('AO'); io.draw(0); return; }\r\n      io.drive('AO', ao, 1);\r\n      io.draw(v / (10000 + r));\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\r\n      return [`${force.toFixed(2)} N pressing: AO ${ao.toFixed(2)} V`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// Limit switch / bumper: COM-NO closed while its roller (or bar) is pushed with 0.5 N or more.\r\nbench.device('limit', (part) => {\r\n  let surface = null;\r\n  try { surface = part.touch('roller'); } catch { surface = part.touch('bar'); }\r\n  let btn = null;\r\n  try { btn = part.control('press'); } catch { /* the bumper has no button */ }\r\n  let pressed = false, presses = 0, force = 0;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      force = surface.force;\r\n      const now = force >= 0.5 || surface.hand || !!btn?.down;\r\n      if (now && !pressed) presses++;\r\n      pressed = now;\r\n      io.connect('COM', 'NO', pressed);\r\n      io.connect('COM', 'NC', !pressed);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      return [`${pressed ? 'pressed: COM-NO closed' : 'not pressed: COM-NC closed'}`, `${presses} presses${force > 0.01 ? `, ${force.toFixed(2)} N on it` : ''}`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// Slide potentiometer: W between GND (knob at -3 cm) and VCC (+3 cm). The run panel's slider moves\r\n// the knob there; then it lets go, so the ball or a drag can move it too.\r\nbench.device('slidepot', (part) => {\r\n  const knob = part.motor('knob');\r\n  const set = part.control('set');\r\n  let lastSet = set.value, holdUntil = 0.5, powered = false, frac = 0.5;\r\n  return {\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      if (set.value !== lastSet) { lastSet = set.value; holdUntil = io.time + 0.6; }\r\n      if (io.time < holdUntil) knob.to(((lastSet / 100) * 6 - 3), 5);\r\n      else knob.limp();\r\n      frac = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (knob.position + 3) / 6));\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      powered = v > 0.1;\r\n      if (!powered) { io.release('W'); return; }\r\n      io.drive('W', (io.v('GND') ?? 0) + v * frac, 1);\r\n      io.draw(v / 10000);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      return [`knob at ${Math.round(frac * 100)} %${powered ? '' : ' (no power on VCC/GND)'}`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n\r\n// HX711 + load cell. DT is LOW when a reading is ready (10 a second). The included HX711.h asks\r\n// for it with a message on SCK (the 24 clock pulses, as one message) and gets the 3 bytes back on DT.\r\nbench.device('hx711', (part) => {\r\n  const pan = part.touch('pan');\r\n  const cap = Number(part.params.capacity ?? 5) * 1000; // g\r\n  const PER_GRAM = 420 * (5000 / cap); // (a smaller cell gives more counts per gram)\r\n  const ZERO = 8400; // the empty pan's reading (the pan's own weight, the cell's offset)\r\n  let powered = false, ready = false, nextAt = 0, grams = 0, reads = 0, gain = 128, down = false, raw = ZERO, reply = null;\r\n  const measure = () => {\r\n    let g = grams * PER_GRAM;\r\n    if (gain === 64) g /= 2;\r\n    raw = Math.round(ZERO + g + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 60);\r\n    return Math.max(-0x800000, Math.min(0x7fffff, raw));\r\n  };\r\n  return {\r\n    packets(list) {\r\n      for (const p of list) {\r\n        if (p.pin !== 'SCK' || p.proto !== 'data' || !powered) continue;\r\n        const pulses = p.data[0] ?? 25;\r\n        if (pulses >= 60) { down = true; continue; } // (SCK held high: power down)\r\n        down = false;\r\n        if (pulses < 25) continue; // (SCK low again: powered up, nothing asked yet)\r\n        if (!ready) continue; // (not ready: a real one would give garbage)\r\n        gain = pulses === 26 ? 32 : pulses === 27 ? 64 : 128;\r\n        const v = measure() & 0xffffff;\r\n        reply = [(v >> 16) & 255, (v >> 8) & 255, v & 255];\r\n        ready = false;\r\n        reads++;\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      powered = v >= 2.6;\r\n      // what presses on the pan, as grams (above its capacity, the cell's reading tops out)\r\n      grams = Math.min(cap * 1.1, pan.force / 0.00980665);\r\n      if (!powered || down) { io.release('DT'); io.draw(down ? 0.000001 : 0); ready = false; return; }\r\n      if (io.time >= nextAt && !ready) { ready = true; nextAt = io.time + 0.1; }\r\n      if (reply) { io.send('DT', 'data', reply); reply = null; }\r\n      io.drive('DT', ready ? 0 : v, 1);\r\n      io.draw(0.0015);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!powered) return ['no power'];\r\n      if (down) return ['powered down (scale.power_down())'];\r\n      return [`${grams.toFixed(1)} g on the pan${grams > cap ? ' (over its capacity!)' : ''}`, `${reads} readings`];\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n","sketch":{"HX711.h":{"classes":["HX711"],"code":"// HX711.h (bogde's library): HX711 scale;  scale.begin(DT_PIN, SCK_PIN);  scale.tare();\n//   scale.set_scale(420);  scale.get_units(5) (grams, with that scale);  scale.read() (raw 24 bits).\n// Here the 24 clock pulses go as one message on SCK and the answer comes back on DT (a real HX711\n// is clocked bit by bit; the simulation passes the bits together).\nclass HX711 {\n  constructor() { this.dt = -1; this.sck = -1; this.gain = 128; this.OFFSET = 0; this.SCALE = 1; }\n  begin(dout, sck, gain = 128) {\n    this.dt = dout; this.sck = sck;\n    pinMode(dout, INPUT);\n    pinMode(sck, OUTPUT);\n    digitalWrite(sck, LOW);\n    this.set_gain(gain);\n  }\n  set_gain(g = 128) { this.gain = g === 64 ? 64 : g === 32 ? 32 : 128; }\n  is_ready() { return digitalRead(this.dt) === LOW; }\n  wait_ready(ms = 0) { while (!this.is_ready()) delay(ms || 1); }\n  wait_ready_timeout(timeout = 1000, ms = 1) {\n    const until = millis() + timeout;\n    while (millis() < until) { if (this.is_ready()) return true; delay(ms); }\n    return false;\n  }\n  /** one raw reading (a signed 24-bit number); 0 if the HX711 doesn't answer */\n  read() {\n    if (!this.wait_ready_timeout(1000)) return 0;\n    linkReceive(this.dt, 'data'); // (anything old)\n    linkSend(this.sck, 'data', [this.gain === 64 ? 27 : this.gain === 32 ? 26 : 25]);\n    const until = millis() + 50;\n    while (millis() < until) {\n      const got = linkReceive(this.dt, 'data');\n      if (got.length) {\n        const d = got[got.length - 1].data;\n        let v = (d[0] << 16) | (d[1] << 8) | d[2];\n        if (v & 0x800000) v -= 0x1000000;\n        return v;\n      }\n      delay(1);\n    }\n    return 0;\n  }\n  read_average(times = 10) {\n    let sum = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < times; i++) sum += this.read();\n    return sum / Math.max(1, times);\n  }\n  get_value(times = 1) { return this.read_average(times) - this.OFFSET; }\n  get_units(times = 1) { return this.get_value(times) / this.SCALE; }\n  tare(times = 10) { this.OFFSET = this.read_average(times); }\n  set_scale(s = 1) { this.SCALE = s || 1; }\n  get_scale() { return this.SCALE; }\n  set_offset(o = 0) { this.OFFSET = o; }\n  get_offset() { return this.OFFSET; }\n  power_down() { linkSend(this.sck, 'data', [64]); }\n  power_up() { linkSend(this.sck, 'data', [0]); }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"ttp223","name":"Touch pad (TTP223)","description":"A capacitive touch button: touch its round pad with the ball (hold Shift) or press Touch in the run panel and SIG goes HIGH (while touched; or, with the toggle jumper, each touch flips it). VCC (2-5.5 V), GND, SIG.","swatch":"#d93a3a","mass":1,"params":[{"key":"mode","label":"Jumper","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"momentary","label":"HIGH while touched"},{"value":"toggle","label":"each touch flips it"}]}],"defaults":{"mode":"momentary"},"shape":[{"box":[1.5,0.12,2.4],"at":[0,0.06,0],"color":"#d93a3a"},{"cyl":[0.6,0.04],"at":[0,0.14,0.35],"color":"#e8e1d2","touch":"pad"},{"box":[0.15,0.08,0.15],"at":[0.5,0.16,-0.5],"color":"#e33030","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","SIG","VCC"],"at":[-0.254,0,-1.05],"kinds":{"GND":"gnd","SIG":"out","VCC":"vin"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (2-5.5 V)","vmin":2,"vmax":5.5},"SIG":{"pulled":"down"}}}],"controls":[{"id":"touch","kind":"button","label":"Touch"}],"device":"ttp223"},{"id":"fsr","name":"Force pad (FSR 402 module)","description":"A force-sensing resistor on a little board with its 10k resistor: the harder something presses its round pad, the higher AO (0 V: nothing; about VCC/2 at 1 N; near VCC at 10 N). Press it with the ball, or set a weight on it. VCC, GND, AO (to an analog pin).","swatch":"#2b2b2e","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[2,0.12,3.2],"at":[0,0.06,0],"color":"#1d4fb8"},{"cyl":[0.9,0.06],"at":[0,0.15,0.5],"color":"#2b2b2e","touch":"pad"}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VCC","GND","AO"],"at":[-0.254,0,-1.45],"kinds":{"VCC":"vin","GND":"gnd","AO":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3-5 V)","vmin":2,"vmax":5.5},"AO":{"analog":true}}}],"controls":[{"id":"press","kind":"slider","label":"Press by hand (N)","min":0,"max":20,"step":0.1,"value":0}],"device":"fsr"},{"id":"limit-switch","name":"Limit switch (lever, roller)","description":"A micro switch with a roller lever: when something pushes the roller (about 0.5 N), COM joins NO; otherwise COM joins NC. Robots and 3D printers use them to know they've reached the end. Wire COM to GND and NO to a pin with INPUT_PULLUP: LOW = pressed.","swatch":"#2b2b2e","mass":3,"shape":[{"box":[2,1,1],"at":[0,0.5,0],"color":"#2b2b2e"},{"box":[0.2,0.15,0.25],"at":[0.6,1.07,0],"color":"#d03030","collide":false},{"box":[2.2,0.06,0.4],"at":[0.4,1.35,0],"rot":[0,0,8],"color":"#c9cdd4","collide":false},{"cyl":[0.25,0.4],"at":[1.5,1.55,0],"rot":[90,0,0],"color":"#e0e0e0","touch":"roller"}],"pins":[{"id":"COM","at":[-0.7,0.05,-0.55],"kind":"io"},{"id":"NO","label":"NO (closed when pressed)","at":[0,0.05,-0.55],"kind":"io"},{"id":"NC","label":"NC (closed when not pressed)","at":[0.7,0.05,-0.55],"kind":"io"}],"controls":[{"id":"press","kind":"button","label":"Press"}],"device":"limit"},{"id":"bumper","name":"Bumper switch (robot front)","description":"A limit switch with a wide bumper bar in front: when the robot runs into something, COM joins NO. Glue it to the front of a robot, its bar facing forward (+x). COM to GND, NO to a pin with INPUT_PULLUP: LOW = bumped.","swatch":"#f2c230","mass":6,"shape":[{"box":[1.2,1,1],"at":[0,0.5,0],"color":"#2b2b2e"},{"box":[1.4,0.15,0.25],"at":[0.9,0.5,0],"color":"#c9cdd4","collide":false},{"box":[0.4,1.2,7],"at":[1.8,0.6,0],"color":"#f2c230","touch":"bar"}],"pins":[{"id":"COM","at":[-0.45,0.05,-0.55],"kind":"io"},{"id":"NO","label":"NO (closed when bumped)","at":[0,0.05,-0.55],"kind":"io"},{"id":"NC","label":"NC (closed when not bumped)","at":[0.45,0.05,-0.55],"kind":"io"}],"device":"limit"},{"id":"slide-pot","name":"Slide potentiometer (10k)","description":"A sliding knob: drag its knob (or push it with the ball), or set it with the slider in the run panel. W is between GND (knob at the left) and VCC (at the right): read it with analogRead. VCC, GND, W.","swatch":"#2b2b2e","mass":12,"shape":[{"box":[8.5,0.8,1.6],"at":[0,0.4,0],"color":"#2b2b2e"},{"box":[6.4,0.02,0.2],"at":[0,0.81,0],"color":"#555a62","collide":false}],"pins":[{"id":"GND","at":[-3.9,0.05,-0.95],"kind":"gnd"},{"id":"W","label":"W (wiper)","at":[0,0.05,-0.95],"kind":"out","analog":true},{"id":"VCC","at":[3.9,0.05,-0.95],"kind":"vin"}],"moving":[{"id":"knob","mass":2,"shape":[{"box":[0.4,0.5,0.4],"at":[0,1.05,0],"color":"#c9cdd4"},{"box":[0.9,0.6,1.3],"at":[0,1.55,0],"color":"#e8e8e8"}],"joint":{"type":"slide","at":[0,1,0],"axis":[1,0,0],"motor":"servo","force":3,"speed":30,"min":-3,"max":3}}],"controls":[{"id":"set","kind":"slider","label":"Knob (%)","min":0,"max":100,"step":1,"value":50}],"device":"slidepot"},{"id":"scale","name":"Kitchen scale (load cell + HX711)","description":"A 5 kg load cell under a 12 x 12 cm pan, read by an HX711. Put things on the pan (drag them there) and it weighs them: about 420 counts per gram. VCC (2.6-5.5 V), GND, DT and SCK to any two pins. #include <HX711.h>; HX711 scale; scale.begin(DT, SCK); scale.tare(); scale.set_scale(420); scale.get_units(5) (grams).","swatch":"#c9cdd4","mass":300,"params":[{"key":"capacity","label":"Load cell","kind":"select","options":[{"value":"1","label":"1 kg"},{"value":"5","label":"5 kg"},{"value":"20","label":"20 kg"}]}],"defaults":{"capacity":"5"},"shape":[{"box":[12,1.6,12],"at":[0,0.8,0],"color":"#2b2d33"},{"box":[12.4,0.3,12.4],"at":[0,1.85,0],"color":"#c9cdd4","touch":"pan"},{"box":[2,0.12,2.6],"at":[0,1.66,-6.9],"color":"#2a6b3a","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","DT","SCK","VCC"],"at":[-0.381,0,-7.6],"kinds":{"GND":"gnd","DT":"out","SCK":"in","VCC":"vin"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (2.6-5.5 V)","vmin":2.6,"vmax":5.5}}}],"device":"hx711"}],"examples":[{"name":"Kitchen scale","description":"A scale and some weights: press Run, then drag a weight onto the pan. The board tares it at the start and prints grams; press the pan with the ball (Shift) and watch the reading.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Kitchen scale","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-14,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"scale","type":"touch-and-force/scale","name":"Scale","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[4,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"w100","type":"block","name":"100 g weight","params":{"w":2.6,"h":2,"d":2.45,"material":"steel","color":"#9aa3ad"},"parent":null,"pos":[-4,0,12],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"w250","type":"block","name":"250 g weight","params":{"w":3.4,"h":3,"d":3.13,"material":"steel","color":"#7f8893"},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,13],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"apple","type":"ball","name":"Apple","params":{"r":3.4,"material":"wood","color":"#c8312b"},"parent":null,"pos":[9,0,13],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"scale","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"scale","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"scale","pin":"DT"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"scale","pin":"SCK"},"color":"#4a90e2"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Kitchen scale: a load cell and an HX711. Press Run, then drag a weight onto the pan: the grams\n// show in the serial monitor (press Plot to graph them).\n#include <HX711.h>\n\n#define DT 2\n#define SCK 3\n\nHX711 scale;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  scale.begin(DT, SCK);\n  Serial.println(\"Taring: keep the pan empty...\");\n  scale.tare(10);          // what the empty pan reads is zero\n  scale.set_scale(420);    // counts per gram (found by weighing something known)\n  Serial.println(\"Ready: put something on the pan\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  float grams = scale.get_units(5);\n  if (abs(grams) < 0.5) grams = 0;\n  Serial.print(\"weight:\");\n  Serial.println(grams, 1);\n  delay(500);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Touch lamp and dimmer","description":"Touch the pad (Shift + the ball, or Touch in the run panel) to switch the LED on and off; drag the slide pot's knob to dim it; squeeze the force pad and its reading is printed.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Touch lamp and dimmer","parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"maker-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"pad","type":"touch-and-force/ttp223","name":"Touch pad","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,-6],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"pot","type":"touch-and-force/slide-pot","name":"Dimmer","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[6,0,2],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"fsr","type":"touch-and-force/fsr","name":"Force pad","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[2,0,9],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"led","type":"led","name":"Lamp","params":{"color":"yellow"},"parent":null,"pos":[-10,0,8],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"pad","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"pot","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"pot","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"A0"},"b":{"uid":"pot","pin":"W"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"fsr","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"fsr","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"A1"},"b":{"uid":"fsr","pin":"AO"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"A"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"led","pin":"K"},"color":"#2b2d33"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Touch lamp: touch the pad (hold Shift and touch it with the ball, or press Touch in the run panel)\n// to switch the lamp; drag the slide pot's knob to dim it; press the force pad and see how hard.\n#define PAD 2\n#define LAMP 15\n#define DIMMER A0\n#define FORCE A1\n\nbool on = false;\nbool wasTouched = false;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(PAD, INPUT);\n  pinMode(LAMP, OUTPUT);\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  bool touched = digitalRead(PAD) == HIGH;\n  if (touched && !wasTouched) {\n    on = !on;\n    Serial.println(on ? \"lamp on\" : \"lamp off\");\n  }\n  wasTouched = touched;\n\n  int level = analogRead(DIMMER);          // 0 .. 4095\n  int brightness = map(level, 0, 4095, 0, 255);\n  analogWrite(LAMP, on ? brightness : 0);\n\n  int force = analogRead(FORCE);\n  if (force > 100) {\n    Serial.print(\"squeeze:\");\n    Serial.println(force);\n  }\n  delay(50);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}},{"name":"Bumper rover","description":"A rover with a bumper: it drives until it runs into the wall, backs up and turns. Press Run; drag the wall somewhere else.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Bumper rover","parts":[{"uid":"chassis","type":"plate","name":"Chassis","params":{"w":12,"h":0.3,"d":9,"material":"plastic","color":"#8fa3b8"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,4.4,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"motorR","type":"motor-tt","name":"Right motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[0,-0.15,3.55],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"motorL","type":"motor-tt","name":"Left motor","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[3.2,-0.15,-3.55],"rot":[1,0,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelR","type":"wheel","name":"Right wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.2},"parent":{"uid":"motorR","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,1,0,0]},{"uid":"wheelL","type":"wheel","name":"Left wheel","params":{"r":3.3,"width":2.6,"grip":1.2},"parent":{"uid":"motorL","body":"hub"},"pos":[0,0.45,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"battery","type":"battery-18650","name":"Batteries","params":{"count":"2","charge":100},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-2.2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"brain","type":"maker-board","name":"Brain","params":{"usb":false},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[2.6,0.15,0],"rot":[0,-0.7071,0,0.7071]},{"uid":"driver","type":"drv8833","name":"Motor driver","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"battery","body":"body"},"pos":[0,2,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"caster","type":"caster","name":"Caster","params":{"r":1.57},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[-4.6,-0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,1,0]},{"uid":"bumper","type":"touch-and-force/bumper","name":"Bumper","params":{},"parent":{"uid":"chassis","body":"body"},"pos":[5.2,0.15,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"wallE","type":"block","name":"Wall (east)","params":{"w":2,"h":12,"d":82,"material":"wood","color":"#9b7b5b"},"parent":null,"pos":[40,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"wallW","type":"block","name":"Wall (west)","params":{"w":2,"h":12,"d":82,"material":"wood","color":"#9b7b5b"},"parent":null,"pos":[-40,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"wallN","type":"block","name":"Wall (north)","params":{"w":78,"h":12,"d":2,"material":"wood","color":"#9b7b5b"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,-40],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true},{"uid":"wallS","type":"block","name":"Wall (south)","params":{"w":78,"h":12,"d":2,"material":"wood","color":"#9b7b5b"},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,40],"rot":[0,0,0,1],"pinned":true}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"VM"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"+"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"VIN"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"battery","pin":"-"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GND2"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP2"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AIN1"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP3"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AIN2"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP5"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BIN1"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP6"},"b":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BIN2"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motorR","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"AOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motorR","pin":"M-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BOUT1"},"b":{"uid":"motorL","pin":"M+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"driver","pin":"BOUT2"},"b":{"uid":"motorL","pin":"M-"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w13","a":{"uid":"bumper","pin":"COM"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w14","a":{"uid":"bumper","pin":"NO"},"b":{"uid":"brain","pin":"GP10"},"color":"#e8c547"}],"programs":{"brain":{"lang":"arduino","source":"#define AIN1 2    // right motor (through the DRV8833)\n#define AIN2 3\n#define BIN1 5    // left motor\n#define BIN2 6\n\nvoid motor(int in1, int in2, int speed) {\n  if (speed >= 0) { analogWrite(in1, speed); analogWrite(in2, 0); }\n  else            { analogWrite(in1, 0);     analogWrite(in2, -speed); }\n}\n\nvoid drive(int left, int right) {   // -255 .. 255\n  motor(BIN1, BIN2, left);\n  motor(AIN2, AIN1, right);         // the right motor faces the other way\n}\n\n// Bumper rover: drives ahead until its bumper hits something, then backs up and turns away.\n#define BUMPER 10   // the bumper's NO; its COM is on GND, so LOW = bumped\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  pinMode(BUMPER, INPUT_PULLUP);\n  Serial.println(\"bumper rover ready\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  if (digitalRead(BUMPER) == LOW) {\n    Serial.println(\"bump! backing up\");\n    drive(-200, -200);\n    delay(500);\n    drive(200, -200);    // turn\n    delay(400);\n  } else {\n    drive(200, 200);\n  }\n  delay(20);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}